2026-02-10 02:58:54,142 - DocumentGraderNode - INFO: Retrieved document What Are Some Examples of Derivatives?

Common examples of derivatives include futures contracts, options contracts, and credit default swaps. Beyond these, there's a vast quantity of derivative contracts tailored to meet the needs of a diverse range of counterparties. In fact, because many derivatives are traded over the counter (OTC), they can, in principle, be infinitely customized. is relevant
